 "prediction_check": "after 2024 the 30 day share fell; after 2026-04-15 it did not move outside its interval (30 day shares 0.8015947396266344, 0.43556961072208417, 0.41418786534319996 for the three periods).",
 "method": "The first NVD analysis is the first Initial Analysis, Reanalysis or Modified Analysis event in the NVD change history. The share within k days counts, among the CVEs published at least k days before the data cut, those whose first analysis came within k days. Intervals are a cluster bootstrap by filer, 2,000 resamples, 95 percent percentile intervals; the period differences use one shared draw and are corrected as one Benjamini-Hochberg family at 0.05. The median days to analysis is given two ways: among the CVEs the NVD did analyze, and as a Kaplan-Meier median that counts a CVE not analyzed by the cut as censored at its follow-up, which is the honest median when many are never analyzed.",
 "sql": "-- Q1: CVEs published per month since January 2020, rejected excluded, and the share the NVD\n-- analyzed within 7, 30 and 90 days among those old enough to be judged at each horizon.\nselect\n    published_month,\n    count(*) as cves,\n    count(analyzed_7d) as judged_7d,\n    avg(cast(analyzed_7d as integer)) as share_7d,\n    count(analyzed_30d) as judged_30d,\n    avg(cast(analyzed_30d as integer)) as share_30d,\n    count(analyzed_90d) as judged_90d,\n    avg(cast(analyzed_90d as integer)) as share_90d,\n    count(first_analysis_at) as analyzed,\n    median(days_to_analysis) as median_days_if_analyzed,\n    count(*) filter (where analysis_undated) as analysis_undated\nfrom gold.mart_backlog_q1\ngroup by published_month\norder by published_month"
}
